FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://polls.example.com

# Polls API

Hand-authored reconstruction of the shape of the canonical Apiary "Polls"
tutorial API (questions with choices that can be voted on); no third-party
text copied.

## Questions Collection [/questions]

+ Parameters
    + page (number, optional) - Page of results to return.

### List questions [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (array[Question])

### Create a question [POST]

+ Request (application/json)
    + Attributes (QuestionRequest)

+ Response 201 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Question)

## Question [/questions/{question_id}]

+ Parameters
    + question_id (number, required) - Identifier of the question.

### View a question detail [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Question)

+ Response 404

## Choice [/questions/{question_id}/choices/{choice_id}]

+ Parameters
    + question_id (number, required) - Identifier of the question.
    + choice_id (number, required) - Identifier of the choice.

### Vote on a choice [POST]

+ Response 201 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Choice)

# Data Structures

## Question (object)
+ question: `Favourite programming language?` (string, required) - The question text.
+ published_at: `2026-01-05T08:40:51Z` (string, required) - Publication timestamp.
+ url: `/questions/1` (string, required) - Canonical URL of the question.
+ choices: `[]` (array, required) - Available answer choices.

## QuestionRequest (object)
+ question: `Favourite programming language?` (string, required) - The question text.
+ choices: `[]` (array, required) - Choice texts to create.

## Choice (object)
+ choice: `Python` (string, required) - Choice text.
+ url: `/questions/1/choices/1` (string, required) - Canonical URL of the choice.
+ votes: 3 (number, required) - Number of votes cast so far.
